Jensen marked 'slides only — not recorded'; Brad Sturt and Song Ma marked 'no recording or slides posted' rather than silently dropped or invented. The five-thread synthesis is genuine analysis, not a table of contents. Coverage-honesty and inferential restraint in the full summary are a real asset — the very discipline that is missing one layer up. This finding exists to prevent the diagnosis from reading as uniformly negative: the core archive earns 'sound.'\",\n      \"verdict\": \"Preserve the full summary's coverage-honesty discipline and propagate it upward to the exec brief; it is the template the higher-stakes layer should follow.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"F5\",\n      \"kind\": \"diagnose\",\n      \"severity\": \"moderate\",\n      \"rung\": \"OBSERVED\",\n      \"reasoning\": \"Secrets hygiene. Per git status, .research-symposium/ is untracked AND not ignored (shown as '??'), so a single 'git add -A' would stage it. It contains an authenticated session cookie and session state (cookies.json, sess.json) plus auth-capture artifacts (login_capture.py, auth_log.txt, login_log.txt, request_code.py, verify_code.py). The signed session cookie has Max-Age 86400 (per the effort's own RESEARCH_REPORT.md), so live exposure is likely already expired — but committing or sharing the repo would leak credential material and the scraping toolchain.\",\n      \"verdict\": \"Add .research-symposium/ (or at least cookies.json, sess.json, *_log.txt, *capture*) to .gitignore now and scrub it from any commit/share; confirm the cookie is expired/revoked.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"A1\",\n      \"kind\": \"anticipate\",\n      \"severity\": \"moderate\",\n      \"rung\": \"CLAIMED\",\n      \"future_state_condition\": \"Months after the exec brief lands, the recommended summer faculty study group is working through the ordered course list (Toubia -> Ramakrishnan -> NYU Foundations of AI Agents, with Boussioux as supplement) as if it were a fixed syllabus, and a noticeable share of the specific tools/models/flows demoed (GPT-4o, particular n8n graphs, specific Lovable/Replit behaviors) has already shifted under them — making parts of the curated path stale at the moment of execution.\",\n      \"enabling_assumption\": \"The brief frames 'work through the openly available courses' as durable content rather than as fast-moving exemplars, and offers no refresh/triage mechanism — even though multiple speakers in the very same archive flagged the short half-life ('the models keep improving and may eventually erode that scaffolding'; 'whether the human-advantage category is shrinking').\",\n      \"reasoning\": \"Premortem on the single recommended action. The author has not yet priced the gap between the artifact's recommendation cadence (a multi-week summer study group) and the field's change cadence (which the archive itself documents as rapid). Subject is the one effort's own recommendation; no cross-path regret pricing.\",\n      \"verdict\": \"Reframe the recommendation around durable skills the archive surfaces (specify/verify/iterate; 'where the human sits'; discernment) and treat named courses/tools as illustrative, with an explicit 're-check tools before the session' step.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"A2\",\n      \"kind\": \"anticipate\",\n      \"severity\": \"moderate\",\n      \"rung\": \"CLAIMED\",\n      \"future_state_condition\": \"A reader (a Dean, or one of the cited faculty) spot-checks a single figure in the exec brief, hits the CAiSEY 3,000-vs-4,100 or the Ipeirotis $15-vs-$3 mismatch, and silently discounts the credibility of the entire 'verified' archive — converting the effort's central rigor asset into a liability.\",\n      \"enabling_assumption\": \"The exec brief ships with the unreconciled numbers positioned next to the 'verified transcripts' framing, so the reader applies the (real, narrow) transcription guarantee to the (unguaranteed) synthesis layer and judges the whole by its weakest, most-quo