te both values with their timepoints/source or remove the precision.\",\n      \"what_would_refute_it\": \"If the divergent figures are demonstrably the same metric at two dates and the audience would read them as an update rather than a contradiction (i.e., the inconsistency is only apparent), the pass adds little beyond a one-line dating note.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"E2\",\n      \"value_if_true\": \"high\",\n      \"severity\": \"major\",\n      \"rung\": \"OBSERVED\",\n      \"reasoning\": \"Extend the provenance stamp to the consumed artifact: attach to the exec brief a one-line scope note stating what 'verified' does and does not certify, and explicitly tag every exec-brief claim that is not transcript-grounded (the WSJ citation; Song Ma / Brad Sturt specifics for un-posted talks) as separately sourced and its verification status. Closes F2; gives the reader an honest map of which claims carry the guarantee.\",\n      \"verdict\": \"Add the scope note and per-claim sourcing tags; verify or downgrade the out-of-chain claims.\",\n      \"what_would_refute_it\": \"If every added exec-brief claim is in fact independently verified and the intended audience already reads 'verified transcripts' as narrowly scoped to transcription, the scope note is redundant.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"E3\",\n      \"value_if_true\": \"medium\",\n      \"severity\": \"moderate\",\n      \"rung\": \"OBSERVED\",\n      \"reasoning\": \"Position the local archive (videos/, transcripts/whisper/, slides) as the durable system of record and snapshot/permalink the external URLs the deliverables cite (the-ai-list.io, leobix.us/genai, genaiwithleo.com, demo and WSJ links, symposium.guetta.com), since the source site already shows missing materials and access is gated by an expiring session cookie. Protects against link rot that would hollow out the references over time.\",\n      \"verdict\": \"Archive/snapshot cited external URLs and label the local copy as the canonical arc